Heading along the Battlements~
   You are heading along the southern half of the battlements on the eastern
wall.  Seagulls circle overhead, and you are puzzling at their presence when
you suddenly remember the river of Fairhaven runs just south east of here.  
Looking over the crenelations, you see it flowing swiftly along, parallel to
the south wall, heading off into a thick forest.  A door to the north leads
into the southern tower, eastern gatehouse.    
